        "project_name": "490/499 Illinois Street (UCSF Wayne and Gladys Valley Center for Vision & Alexandria Center for Science and Technology)",
        "site": "Mission Bay South",
        "status": "complete",
        "use": "institutional",
        "geometry_type": "real",
        "digitized_from": "DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF3940003); names/addresses from OpenStreetMap ways 84821715 (490 Illinois St) and 84821722 (499 Illinois St).",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-19 for Mission Bay's block-by-block reconciliation pass, cross-checking OCII's own numbered Land Use Map (Dec 2019) against everything already tracked, as two separate records: 490 Illinois St (UCSF Wayne and Gladys Valley Center for Vision, a 12-story tower with a 5-story south wing and a garden-topped 3-story north wing, ~75,000 sq ft of parking for 200+ vehicles, opened 2020, ~$237M) and 499 Illinois St (Alexandria Center for Science and Technology, a 6-story, ~450,000 sq ft biotechnology building completed 2008, where UCSF leased ~90% of the space for over a decade before purchasing the building outright from Alexandria Real Estate Equities). MERGED 2026-09-22 per the owner's direction: both share the same DataSF Building Footprints mblr (SF3940003) -- one Assessor block-lot pairing, described together as a connected 490-499 Illinois campus in commercial listings -- so tracking them as two separate records double-counted one real estate holding. Combined into one MultiPolygon (the two building footprints remain geometrically distinct pieces, ~12m apart, not touching) under this project's own OCII block number X4.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL -- surveyed DataSF Building Footprints outline (mblr SF3940003), names/addresses from OpenStreetMap; not a hand trace or plan estimate. UCSF's own occupancy at 499 Illinois St (leased, then purchased) versus outright ownership at 490 Illinois St is not distinguished in this single combined record -- see the digitization_method above for each wing's own history.",
        "notes": "OCII plan block X4 (a plan-era open-space number absorbed into this final building complex, per docs/briefs/mission_bay_block_inventory.csv). UCSF Health also operates a Reproductive Health clinic on 499 Illinois St's 6th floor.",
        "source_doc_urls": [
